The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md (about 11 KB), but it is not committed. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit command did nothing (the || true let it pass). I didn't force-add it; the planner reads the file from disk.

Main points for the planner:

• Build and history: the harness confirmed the build at session start. The v0.4.0 binary answers -p correctly ("PONG", exit 0). The last 4 finished evolve runs and the last 5 CI runs all passed, the current evolve run is still going, and there were no reverts in 14 days.
• @yuanhao asked for a class fix on #1132 (09:39Z, just before this session). He wants one shared fix instead of one verb per session: route every shell verb that takes operands through verb_flags, have the helper return the flag/operand split it already computes, and add one test that walks the dispatch table. He says this would close #1132 and #1133 together and lets me argue for per-verb fixes if I think they're better. The planner should either take this or answer him on #1132 by name.
• New bug: `yoyo grep` can't search for a pattern starting with a dash outside a git repo. In a non-git temp dir, yoyo grep -- --count y.txt and yoyo grep -- -x y.txt (also with -c and -C 1) print "No matches found." even though the file contains the text. The same commands inside a git repo find it.
  • Cause: the git branch puts -- before the pattern. The three branches that call the system grep (around lines 1534, 1671 and 1845 of commands_search.rs) don't, so grep reads the pattern as one of its own options.
  • This corrects #1133's diagnosis for grep: the problem isn't the handler re-reading the raw arguments. The shared helper alone won't fix it, so it should be part of the #1132 work and reported to him there. The outline -- --all half of #1133 still fails as filed.
• Other things I reproduced:
  • blame --bogus hands the flag to git's own error.
  • test --bogus passes it on to cargo test (#1132).
  • map, docs, risk, lint and skill still print chat-style /command advice in the terminal (#1127).
• Two files are close to the size limit that fails `cargo test`:
  • commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 2036 lines and has no recorded exception; 14 more lines fails the build.
  • config.rs is 4851 lines against its recorded 4762; 11 more lines fails it.
• Research: I scanned Claude Code 2.1.317–318 and Codex 0.165–0.166 and saved the notes to yopedia. The idea most worth copying is Claude Code's change making claude -p exit 1 when a write to disk fails. That's the same kind of problem as #1026 (one-shot mode exiting 0 after something went wrong).

The assessment suggests #1132 + #1133 as the main task, plus one smaller item: #1126, #1127/#1128 or #1135.
